A||||5||Wannabe||Northstar "Fitting"||||1||
Z||000000||Wannabe||10-01-2001||06:18 PM||||Anybody working on Northstar swaps, have you had a chance to test fit the engines into the bay yet? I've heard tow stories now, either the engine fits with no problems, or the trunk and firewall need to be cut and modified to make room. Which is it? <P>BTW, this may be the final deciding factory for me personally between a SBC or the Northstar. The obvious benefit of the Northstar is weight savings and perhaps inital cost of install. The major benefit of the SBC is that the swap has been well developed and documented, and so, ought to  be the closest thing to a nuts and bolts install - plus there is some fun in shopping for all the goodies that are available for the sbc  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||10-01-2001||09:40 PM||||Wannabe, the engine fits with little cutting <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  If you leave the alternator on in the stock location you have to knock in the fire wall on the passenger side bottom.  Also the passenger side hinge must be cut and reinforced (The hinge will be cut in half) and if it is not reinforced the force of a gas strut (to hold up the deck) will cause the trunk to shift (I learned the hard way <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)  Also on the passenger side, the bottom of the strut tower mount on the engine bay side has to be trimmed (a very little).  That is it (besides the modifications of the craddle)!  My engine went in and out alot over the week-end, each time making little changes.  The one that really had me scratching my head was the alternator.  I couldn't tell it was touching and I couldn't figure out why the cradle bolts weren't lining up!  If you want to see more about a Northstar see my web page in my signature, and please feel free to ask.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wannabe||10-01-2001||10:17 PM||||Actually Jay, it was Fiero shop that told me the fitting was a nightmare. The other accounts claimed no problems. Of course, I put a lot of credence into what Fiero Shop says as they know what they are doing. They also said the trunk had to be cut out. As it goes, my mind is now 80/20 towards doing a small block swap, but until money changes hands for an engine, anything can happen  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||10-02-2001||12:18 AM||||You'll have to cut and weld some on the passenger side decklid hinge, and that's about it if move the alternator (like I did.)<P>All in all, it's easier to put in than a 350 by a huge ammount.<P>People seem afraid of the northstar, I don't know why.  It's an all aluminum v8 that BOLTS to the fiero tranny and fits in the engine with absolutely no frame cutting.<P>Don't be afraid, the northstar loves you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>(and is just a really nice engine to tinker on, you can just feel the engineering and 'clean sheet' design philosophy that went into it.)<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||Wannabe||10-02-2001||09:40 AM||||I supose some of the fear of Northstar swaps comes from the $5000 or so that some places charge just for installation. Given the information that's starting to surface about how straight forward the install might be, it's hard to understand the big buck charges.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||10-02-2001||12:27 PM||||Ben..<P>I don't think fitting the engine is the problem that scares people..it's the wiring.<P>What about issues with clutches and thrust surfaces and such? The N* wasn't designed to have a manual tranny , how are you addressing that?<P>I would love N* , but for track and autocross a lofty shifting auto is not the way to go.<P>Enlighten me!<P>JM ||||reg||1
